Cross apache24 runs a host copy of pcre2-config.

In a cross build the httpd configure script looks only for
${target_alias}-pcre2-config, and pkgsrc sets no target_alias, so it
checked for "-pcre2-config" and stopped at "pcre(2)-config for libpcre
not found". The installed pcre2-config is the target's, under the target
prefix that the build host does not have. The pcre2 buildlink3 file sets
PCRE2_CONFIG to a host copy in cross builds and to the installed script
in native builds; apache24 passes it to configure as PCRE_CONFIG, which
configure takes as the result of its search.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.
Test: profiles/common-build-tools/tests/apache24-pcre2-config.sh

--- a/www/apache24/Makefile
+++ b/www/apache24/Makefile
@@ -31,6 +31,7 @@
 CONFIGURE_ARGS+=	--with-port=80
 CONFIGURE_ENV+=		perlbin=${PERL5:Q}
 CONFIGURE_ENV+=		ac_cv_path_RSYNC=/nonexistent
+CONFIGURE_ENV+=		PCRE_CONFIG=${PCRE2_CONFIG:Q}
 
 .include "../../mk/compiler.mk"
 
